{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 68, :comments ["<b>In ships.</b> In boats — into captivity." "<b>And you shall sell yourselves there to your enemies.</b> You will seek to be sold to them as slaves and maidservants." "<b>And none shall buy.</b> For they will decree upon you killing and destruction." "<b>And you shall sell yourselves.</b> In la'az איפורוונדרי\"ץ וו\"ש. And it is not tenable to interpret ״וְהִתְמַכַּרְתֶּם״ in the sense of 'and you were sold' through other sellers, because it is stated after it ״וְאֵין קֹנֶה״."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {3 "The la'az איפורוונדרי\"ץ וו\"ש appears to be Old French 'je me pourvendrai' or similar, in the reflexive/reciprocal sense; the exact reading is uncertain."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:48:47.195795692Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}